I=\frac{P}{4 \pi r^2}=\frac{1}{4 \pi .1^2}=\frac{1}{4 \pi} \mathrm{W} / \mathrm{m}^2

Power absorbed by the circular plates of radius $1 Å$ is; $P=I \times$ Area of plate,

\begin{aligned}
